WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.869
-Thank you for coming back
to our show.

00:00:02.869 --> 00:00:04.704
I'm so excited that you're here,

00:00:04.704 --> 00:00:07.740
and I just read some amazing
things about you, all true.

00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:11.544
And there was more stuff
I wanted to talk about.

00:00:11.544 --> 00:00:13.913
I didn't know -- you have
an Oscar nomination

00:00:13.913 --> 00:00:15.414
for Best Original Song.
-Yes. Yes.

00:00:15.414 --> 00:00:16.782
-You're the first woman
to be nominated

00:00:16.782 --> 00:00:18.584
for a Producer of the Year
Grammy.

00:00:18.584 --> 00:00:20.986
-Yes.
-You have 27 top ten hits.

00:00:20.986 --> 00:00:23.389
-Yes.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:23.389 --> 00:00:26.225
-You have the record for most
consecutive Top 10 hits

00:00:26.225 --> 00:00:29.128
on the U.S. Billboard Hot 100
Chart by a female artist.

00:00:29.128 --> 00:00:31.630
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:31.630 --> 00:00:34.434
And you're the first and only
artist in history to have

00:00:34.434 --> 00:00:36.769
seven top five hits
from one album.

00:00:36.769 --> 00:00:38.905
You are unbelievable.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:38.905 --> 00:00:40.406
You're iconic.

00:00:40.406 --> 00:00:42.575
Just to tell you some nice
things about you.

00:00:42.575 --> 00:00:44.410
-Thank you.
-Is it embarrassing?

00:00:44.410 --> 00:00:46.079
-Yes.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:46.079 --> 00:00:47.680
-Sorry about that.

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:50.383
I want to talk about
so many things.

00:00:50.383 --> 00:00:52.685
"Control" was your first
number one album.

00:00:52.685 --> 00:00:54.420
-Yes.
-Before that, you were more,

00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:56.188
like, into acting
and doing that.

00:00:56.188 --> 00:00:58.124
But what made that album
different?

00:00:58.124 --> 00:00:59.592
And what do you remember
about that album?

00:00:59.592 --> 00:01:03.596
-Oh, gosh, that was me
coming into adulthood.

00:01:03.596 --> 00:01:05.264
-Yeah.

00:01:05.264 --> 00:01:08.368
-Being a kid, a teenager,
going to Minneapolis.

00:01:08.368 --> 00:01:10.070
Being with Jimmy and Terry
and --

00:01:10.070 --> 00:01:12.004
-Oh, yeah.
Jimmy Jam and Terry Lewis.

00:01:12.004 --> 00:01:13.439
-Yes.
-Absolutely.

00:01:13.439 --> 00:01:15.408
What would you guys get into
over there in Minneapolis?

00:01:15.408 --> 00:01:18.077
[ Laughter ]

00:01:18.077 --> 00:01:20.613
-I was very sheltered,

00:01:20.613 --> 00:01:23.616
and I went to Minneapolis
with a friend, a school friend.

00:01:23.616 --> 00:01:26.886
And --
a good kid, good kid.

00:01:26.886 --> 00:01:29.188
Didn't get into much trouble.
-Okay.

00:01:29.188 --> 00:01:31.524
-But I had my moments,

00:01:31.524 --> 00:01:34.060
or they gave me my moments,
I should say.

00:01:34.060 --> 00:01:36.162
-How did they give you
your moments?

00:01:36.162 --> 00:01:39.031
-You know, the drinking age
I think is 18, 19

00:01:39.031 --> 00:01:40.600
in Minneapolis.

00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:43.802
So we went out one night
and they gave me some ice cream.

00:01:43.802 --> 00:01:47.540
I think it's called Brandy
Alexander ice cream.

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:48.708
-Wow.

00:01:48.708 --> 00:01:50.910
-Well, it had a lot of brandy
in it.

00:01:50.910 --> 00:01:52.712
[ Laughter ]
-Really?

00:01:52.712 --> 00:01:56.182
-Yes, and I -- I got messed up.
-Yeah.

00:01:56.182 --> 00:01:58.084
[ Laughter ]
-I -- I --

00:01:58.084 --> 00:02:01.354
-You know, I never had a serious
drink until I was 23.

00:02:01.354 --> 00:02:02.955
-Is that right?
-Yeah, that's --

00:02:02.955 --> 00:02:04.891
-Did you get any work
done that night?

00:02:04.891 --> 00:02:06.492
-No.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:06.492 --> 00:02:07.694
-Didn't work out?
-No.

00:02:07.694 --> 00:02:09.061
-Not a good thing to do at all.
-No.

00:02:09.061 --> 00:02:10.830
-Do you have a favorite line
or favorite lyric?

00:02:10.830 --> 00:02:14.199
Is there one lyric that everyone
always just yells to you?

00:02:14.199 --> 00:02:15.701
-Oh, gosh.

00:02:15.701 --> 00:02:17.336
"Miss Jackson
if you're nasty."

00:02:17.336 --> 00:02:19.071
-Yeah. That's it right there.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:19.071 --> 00:02:21.941
It has to be, right?
It has to be that.

00:02:21.941 --> 00:02:24.009
-I get it from everybody.
-...Miss Jackson!

00:02:24.009 --> 00:02:25.678
-"Miss Jackson."
[ Laughter ]

00:02:25.678 --> 00:02:27.714
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:27.714 --> 00:02:29.248
It is iconic.
That is a great line.

00:02:29.248 --> 00:02:32.185
-I get it from everyone.
-Really?

00:02:32.185 --> 00:02:35.521
-It doesn't -- entertainers.
-Everyone.

00:02:35.521 --> 00:02:37.023
-Everyone.

00:02:37.023 --> 00:02:40.059
-Did you realize it was going to
become iconic when you sang it?

00:02:40.059 --> 00:02:43.296
-No, I mean, you're just
creating music.

00:02:43.296 --> 00:02:46.398
No, I never did,
and the story is crazy.

00:02:46.398 --> 00:02:47.967
-What was the story?

00:02:47.967 --> 00:02:49.702
-Once again in Minneapolis,

00:02:49.702 --> 00:02:52.872
and my friend and I,
we were on our way --

00:02:52.872 --> 00:02:54.974
I had never taken a dance class.

00:02:54.974 --> 00:02:57.877
So she had this great idea
to take a dance class.

00:02:57.877 --> 00:03:01.481
We were staying downtown
at a hotel, at a loft.

00:03:01.481 --> 00:03:03.716
And walking out of the hotel
there were, like,

00:03:03.716 --> 00:03:06.786
five or six older guys up
against the -- you know,

00:03:06.786 --> 00:03:09.822
standing up against the wall,
and they just basically

00:03:09.822 --> 00:03:12.658
started messing with us.

00:03:12.658 --> 00:03:14.126
And --
-Cat-calling and stuff?

00:03:14.126 --> 00:03:15.194
-Yeah.
-Ooh.

00:03:15.194 --> 00:03:17.196
-And I didn't like it very much.
-No.

00:03:17.196 --> 00:03:21.433
-And I was pretty embarrassed
and I was actually pretty upset.

00:03:21.433 --> 00:03:23.335
And I came back to the studio
that night

00:03:23.335 --> 00:03:25.271
and told Jimmy and Terry
about my experience,

00:03:25.271 --> 00:03:27.306
and it turned into the song
"Nasty."

00:03:27.306 --> 00:03:29.642
-Wow.
That is a crazy story.

00:03:29.642 --> 00:03:31.978
Yeah, cause "My first name
ain't 'Baby.'"

00:03:31.978 --> 00:03:34.413
-"It's Janet."
-"Miss Jackson if you're nasty."

00:03:34.413 --> 00:03:36.182
[ Cheers ]

00:03:36.182 --> 00:03:40.019
It's the best.
[ Applause ]

00:03:40.019 --> 00:03:43.089
We asked your number one fan
in the world, Questlove...

00:03:43.089 --> 00:03:45.024
[ Laughter ]

00:03:45.024 --> 00:03:46.793
I was wondering if he has
any questions for you

00:03:46.793 --> 00:03:48.794
that he would
like to ask you.

00:03:48.794 --> 00:03:50.396
Quest, do you have any questions
you would like to ask

00:03:50.396 --> 00:03:51.631
Miss Jackson?
-Yeah, I always --

00:03:51.631 --> 00:03:54.299
I always wanted to know,
for years you wore

00:03:54.299 --> 00:03:57.269
a key in your earring.

00:03:57.269 --> 00:03:59.605
I guess for your animal cages
or whatever, but...

00:03:59.605 --> 00:04:01.573
-Yes.
-Where is that key?

00:04:01.573 --> 00:04:03.242
Like, what happened to it?

00:04:03.242 --> 00:04:05.844
-I'm pretty sure it's in
storage, in my storage.

00:04:05.844 --> 00:04:07.714
Yes.
-Wait, what? So what is this?

00:04:07.714 --> 00:04:09.782
Why would you wear a key --

00:04:09.782 --> 00:04:13.052
-I never kept a -- what --

00:04:13.052 --> 00:04:14.821
-Key chain?
-A key chain.

00:04:14.821 --> 00:04:17.356
So, and I took care
of the animals.

00:04:17.356 --> 00:04:19.058
We had so many animals
growing up.

00:04:19.058 --> 00:04:20.759
-Really?
And that was your job?

00:04:20.759 --> 00:04:23.696
-Yeah, we had fawn,
mouflon sheep,

00:04:23.696 --> 00:04:27.066
peacocks, a giraffe,

00:04:27.066 --> 00:04:29.202
just all kinds of animals.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:29.202 --> 00:04:31.003
-No, that's just --
no, it's totally relatable.

00:04:31.003 --> 00:04:33.071
Every kid had that.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:33.071 --> 00:04:35.674
-So it was my job to feed them,
to clean them,

00:04:35.674 --> 00:04:36.776
to clean the cages.

00:04:36.776 --> 00:04:39.312
That was my, you know,
my chores.

00:04:39.312 --> 00:04:41.814
-So this is a working key.
-That's a working key.

00:04:41.814 --> 00:04:44.082
-That's amazing.
That's a good question, Quest.

00:04:44.082 --> 00:04:45.551
I like that.
I never knew that.

00:04:45.551 --> 00:04:48.654
-So all through school I wore
hooped earrings.

00:04:48.654 --> 00:04:51.090
-Yeah.
-And I would keep the key

00:04:51.090 --> 00:04:53.526
on my earring
so I wouldn't lose it.

00:04:53.526 --> 00:04:54.893
-Any other questions, Quest?

00:04:54.893 --> 00:04:58.297
-Yeah, in the "Miss You Much"
video, you do that --

00:04:58.297 --> 00:05:00.532
that dancing with the chair
and the hat...

00:05:00.532 --> 00:05:01.734
-Yes.
-...that lands on your foot.

00:05:01.734 --> 00:05:02.735
-Yes.

00:05:02.735 --> 00:05:04.136
-How many takes did that
take for --

00:05:04.136 --> 00:05:05.705
-Oh, gosh.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:05.705 --> 00:05:07.506
Well, you know, it's really
funny that you ask me that

00:05:07.506 --> 00:05:10.376
because we shot --
I don't know how many days,

00:05:10.376 --> 00:05:12.811
'cause that was the long-form
video that we were shooting

00:05:12.811 --> 00:05:14.346
for "Rhythm Nation."

00:05:14.346 --> 00:05:18.617
And I think we shot maybe two,
three days for "Miss You Much."

00:05:18.617 --> 00:05:21.019
But that I think was like
the second day of shooting.

00:05:21.019 --> 00:05:23.823
And it was the 23rd hour,

00:05:23.823 --> 00:05:25.491
something like that,
of shooting.

00:05:25.491 --> 00:05:27.927
-Oh, my gosh.
-And we were so delirious.

00:05:27.927 --> 00:05:31.164
They brought breakfast.
We were eating pancakes.

00:05:31.164 --> 00:05:32.798
We were laughing like crazy.

00:05:32.798 --> 00:05:35.368
And then suddenly we had to do
this routine.

00:05:35.368 --> 00:05:38.004
So it didn't take
many takes to --

00:05:38.004 --> 00:05:39.805
obviously in rehearsal
you get it right.

00:05:39.805 --> 00:05:41.007
But we had some mishaps.

